#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0154 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "Exactly one baseline-flagged record plus one ordinary post-baseline record - the textbook-correct shape, byte-for-byte the shape of the shipped green twin cdisc/CDISC-AD0154/CDISC-AD0154-valid-ADLBC.cdt. The shipped Check asks not is_unique_set(ABLFL, keys=[USUBJID, PARAMCD, BASETYPE]), so the two rows carry the distinct tuples (Y,...) and (N,...) and nothing fires. Pins the leading-key fix (Fix #271, ruling M2-D4): with USUBJID as the name operand the question was asked about the triple (USUBJID, PARAMCD, BASETYPE), which repeats once per visit, so EVERY conformant longitudinal BDS row flagged and this reported 1 violation at row=1."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID   type=Char
col USUBJID   type=Char
col PARAMCD   type=Char
col BASETYPE  type=Char
col ABLFL     type=Char
col AVAL      type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | GLUC | LAST | Y | 10
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | GLUC | LAST | N | 12
